		<notes>
			<note>There are two settings of gatherings B-H and K and one setting of I, L, M, A, and χ. Within
				gathering A, there are two settings of the half title, four states of the title page, and two
				states of the advertisement on A3r. Title page state 1 is found with setting 1 of the half title
				and state 1 of the advertisement. Title page state 2 is found with setting 2 of the
				advertisement and state 1 of the advertisement. Title page states 3 and 4 are found with setting
				2 of the half title and state 2 of the advertisement. These variations in type are illustrated </note>
			<note url="../images/whist.1.p.1-variants.pdf">here</note>
			<note>). </note>
			<note rend="paragraph"/>
			<note>Copies with the first setting of gatherings B-H and K are are included here as first
				editions. All have the first setting of the half title, the first state of the title page, and
				the first state of the adverisement, with exceptions noted. </note>
			<note rend="paragraph"></note>
			<note>Copies with the second setting of gatherings B-H and K are second
				editions (described </note>
			<note url="whist.1.p.1.2.xml">here</note>
			<note>) and have the second setting of the half title, the second through fourth states of the
				title page, and the second state of the advertisement. </note>
			<note rend="paragraph"/>
			<note>There are occasional copies of a first edition with a second setting of one or two gatherings and similarly an occasional second edition with a first setting of one of the gatherings. These anomolies are noted with the respective copies. </note>
			<note>In particular O [Jessel e.641] is included here despite its fourth state title page. The
				rest of the gatherings are first settings, so the book is recorded here as a first edition, even
				though the title page identifies it as a second edition. </note>
		</notes>
